 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 28,
   "y": 54,
   "text": "SOUTH: Poole, Wimborne and the sea. NORTH: Cranborne Chase, Salisbury and Stonehenge. The Wessex Ridgeway runs this way, all the way from Marlborough to the Dorset coast at Lyme Regis."
  },
  {
   "x": 24,
   "y": 50,
   "text": "An Iron Age hill fort with three concentric banks and ditches, with entrances on opposite sides, standing on a chalk ridge near Wimborne. The Romans later built roads that met close by. It is one of several places that have been suggested as the site of King Arthur's victory at Mons Badonicus, though nobody knows.",
   "plaque": "w55e_badbury",
   "title": "Badbury Rings"
  },
  {
   "x": 36,
   "y": 27,
   "text": "A group of Neolithic henges, ring-shaped banks and ditches built about 4,500 years ago. In the 12th century the Normans built a church inside the biggest ring, perhaps to claim a place that was already holy. It was left to decay in the 1700s and stands roofless now, with the sheep for a congregation.",
   "plaque": "w55e_knowlton",
   "title": "Knowlton Circles"
  },
  {
   "x": 26,
   "y": 36,
   "text": "THE WESSEX RIDGEWAY. About 136 miles from Marlborough to Lyme Regis, mostly on old chalk ridgeways and green lanes. Walkers say the Dorset end is the best, and they are all from Dorset."
  },
  {
   "x": 32,
   "y": 24,
   "text": "Augustus Pitt Rivers inherited the Cranborne Chase estates in 1880 and spent the next two decades digging them, Roman villages, barrows and hill forts. He recorded every find in place and published the lot with plans and drawings, which made him one of the founders of modern archaeology. The Larmer Tree Gardens he made for the pleasure of his tenants are still open.",
   "plaque": "w55e_pitt_rivers",
   "title": "General Pitt Rivers"
  },
  {
   "x": 34,
   "y": 6,
   "text": "TOLLARD ROYAL. A village in a fold of the chalk, named for a royal hunting lodge. Pitt Rivers once lived at Rushmore, over the hill. Do take the road slowly. It is lined with deer."
  },
  {
   "x": 26,
   "y": 15,
   "text": "WARDENS. NO THROUGH ROAD. (Bridge inspection.) With thanks for your patience."
  }
 ],
